        <fullName>Menu_Management_16jKj000000Xizb</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>View and update menus and menu items (except pricing).</description>
        <developerName>Menu_Management_16jKj000000Xizb</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>PREREQUISITE: You need the storefrontId and accountId before viewing menus or items.You need to runs transition to the Storefront Management topic so that we can identify the storefront or restaurant that you want to update.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1772044681900</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instructions_0_1772044681900</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>VIEW MENUS: Call Get_Active_Menus with the storefrontId and accountId. Display menu names and descriptions. Ask which menu the merchant wants to explore.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>VIEW ITEMS: Call Get_Menu_Items with the menuId (or storefrontId for all items) plus accountId. Display item name, description, price, calories, and availability status.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>UPDATE ITEMS: You can update description, availability (true/false), calories, and image URL. To update an item, you need its menuItemId from the Get_Menu_Items result, plus the accountId.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>PRICE CHANGES: I do NOT handle price updates. If the merchant wants to change a price, say &quot;Price changes are handled separately. Would you like me to help you update the price for [item name]?&quot; Then use the Pricing Management topic.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>MARK UNAVAILABLE: When a merchant says an item is &quot;sold out&quot; or &quot;86&apos;d&quot;, update the item&apos;s availability to false. Confirm: &quot;I&apos;ve marked [item] as unavailable.&quot;</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>UPLOAD MENU: When a user requests a menu upload, ALWAYS follow these steps IN ORDER:
Step 1: Resolve the storefrontId using query_records. If multiple storefronts match, ask the user to choose.
Step 2: AFTER the storefront is confirmed, PAUSE and collect the file upload using the &apos;menuUpload&apos; input. The menuUpload field renders a file upload UI — you must wait for the user to complete the upload.
Step 3: NEVER invoke Upload_Menu without the menuUpload value provided by the user — it is mandatory. Do NOT fabricate, stub, or pass an empty object for menuUpload.
Step 4: The menuUpload field MUST render the file upload UI before action execution. If it does not render, do NOT proceed.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
