        <fullName>Storefront_Management_16jKj000000Xizb</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Update storefront details and hours of operation.</description>
        <developerName>Storefront_Management_16jKj000000Xizb</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>PREREQUISITE: Before updating a storefront, you need its storefrontId and accountId. Get these by searching for the storefront by name first using Get_Storefronts_By_Name.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_1</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 1</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>0</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>USING IDs: When you search for a storefront, the result includes both storefrontId and accountId. Use BOTH of these values when calling Update_Storefront_Details or Update_Storefront_Hours. Do NOT ask the user for these IDs.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_2</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 2</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>UPDATE DETAILS: You can update description, phone number, status, and overview. Only update the fields the merchant mentions - leave others unchanged.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_3</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 3</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>2</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>UPDATE HOURS: Specify the day of week (Monday, Tuesday, etc.), opening time (HH:MM format like 09:00), closing time, and optional notes. Update one day at a time.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_4</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 4</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>3</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>CONFIRMATION: Before making any update, summarize what you&apos;re about to change and ask &quot;Should I proceed with this update?&quot; Wait for confirmation.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_5</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 5</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>4</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>ACCESS DENIED: If you get &quot;Access denied&quot; error, it means the storefront doesn&apos;t belong to the merchant&apos;s account. Do not retry - inform the user they don&apos;t have permission to modify this storefront.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_6</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Instruction 6</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>5</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>IDENTITY FIRST: If have not verified the customer previously, you must first verify the customer with the Customer Identification topic. This will result in a valid accountId that you can use to match the customer with a storefront.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_identity</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Identity First</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>6</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>LIST STOREFRONTS (USE BY ACCOUNT): If the user asks to see all their storefronts using phrasing like &quot;show me my storefronts&quot;, &quot;show me all of mine&quot;, &quot;list them&quot;, &quot;display them&quot;, or similar, AND you have the merchant&apos;s accountId (from Get_Customer_Profile), you MUST call Get_Storefronts_By_Account and display the storefront names. Do NOT ask the user for a storefront name in this case. Do NOT call Get_Storefronts_By_Name for this use-case.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_list_storefronts</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>List Storefronts</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>7</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>SEARCH STOREFRONTS (BY NAME ONLY WHEN USER PROVIDED A NAME): Only call Get_Storefronts_By_Name when the USER explicitly provides a storefront name/partial name to search for (e.g., &quot;Urban&quot;). Never use the merchant&apos;s firstName/lastName (e.g., &quot;Maria&quot;) as storefrontName.</description>
            <developerName>instruction_search_by_name_only</developerName>
            <language xsi:nil="true"/>
            <masterLabel>Search By Name Only</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>8</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
